{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable","id":709808,"title":"Why are \"Super Friends\" mocked but the Legion of Doom considered reasonable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-19T19:34:36-07:00","id":709808,"title":"Why are \"Super Friends\" mocked but the Legion of Doom considered reasonable?","content":"The Kin mage, the &quot;good&quot; vampire, etc various explanations given for crossover is often mocked as &quot;Super friends' yet the Sabbat hanging out with Pentex, Nephandi just working for Pentex? these are just treated as &quot;reasonable&quot; forms of crossover? Why shouldn't the &quot;bad guys&quot; be just as prone to fracturing? Why aren't they as petty and short sighted in their attempts at destruction as anyone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T19:48:17-07:00","id":709847,"title":"","content":"Because in the &quot;legion of doom&quot; scenario the pc's rarely ever get to see the backstabbing, counter plotting and general self centered behavior that goes on behind the scenes because most tabletop rpg's don't have a &quot;meanwhile at the legion of doom&quot; cut scene.<br /> <br /> It's also assumed that on the &quot;super friends&quot; side all the players will work together for the &quot;greater good&quot;. The werewolf will get along with the vampire no matter the wyurm taint, the fae with the mage regardless of banality.<br /> <br /> More so why do people feel the need to play Y when the rest of the group is playing X in X setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 10-19-2015, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T20:00:59-07:00","id":709858,"title":"","content":"In Werewolf The Apocalypse it is pretty clear that the assorted monsters working for/with Pentex are pretty regularly turning on each other. The whole &quot;Heads of the Hydra&quot; thing out-and-out says it. Black Spiral Dancers, Nephandi, Sabbat and Evil Fae etc are all pretty &quot;political&quot; and dont like one another for the most part.<br /> <br /> Now if you subscribe to the concept that the Syndicates &quot;Special Projects Division&quot; <i>is </i>Pentex, the cohesion that does exists makes some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-19-2015, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T07:47:38-07:00","id":710532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=709858#post709858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Werewolf The Apocalypse it is pretty clear that the assorted monsters working for/with Pentex are pretty regularly turning on each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex is not the sum total of all Werewolf antagonists, even on the Wyrm's side. I'm quite perplexed why anyone still jumps to name them first and foremost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole &quot;Heads of the Hydra&quot; thing out-and-out says it. Black Spiral Dancers, Nephandi, Sabbat and Evil Fae etc are all pretty &quot;political&quot; and dont like one another for the most part.<br /> <br /> Now if you subscribe to the concept that the Syndicates &quot;Special Projects Division&quot; <i>is </i>Pentex, the cohesion that does exists makes some sense. </div> </div> </div>But that's not quite the same kind of cohesion. It's more the Wyrm taking some unwitting Weaver-ish folk for a ride, whereas cohesion in the style of the Legion of Doom is all of the explicitly designated &quot;bad guy&quot; splats in the same room; the Technocracy is an antagonistic foil, not in the same league as the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:52:36-07:00","id":710905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=710532#post710532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex is not the sum total of all Werewolf antagonists, even on the Wyrm's side. I'm quite perplexed why anyone still jumps to name them first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liam mentioned Pentex twice when he posed the initial question. Thats why I mentioned it.<br /> <br /> The thing about Pentex, unlike most of the other organizations in the White Wolf books, is that it incorporates the supernatural life with a day job. Characters associated with one of Pentex subsidiaries have a paycheck from a company that will accommodate the weird part of their lives. And for a supernatural being, thats a big deal. Most of the villain-types aren't cackling madmen all of the time (some are of course). And it they want anything like a &quot;normal&quot; life, they will have to put aside their differences to maintain their status in the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-21-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T11:29:26-07:00","id":711014,"title":"","content":"Depending on which side of the story one is on, the &quot;bad guys&quot; present a unified front because their selfish, greedy, manipulative desires and behaviors. They have no false veneer of civility to cover their actions, and every party knows the other is going to try to screw them over eventually - it just depends on how much mileage they can squeeze out of each other before that happens. When one is playing the more traditional &quot;good guy&quot; roles in the WoD, the antagonists appear to work together because their goals are nearly the same. This changes when ones plays the &quot;bad guys&quot; - the &quot;good guys&quot; don't work together (or work together well), and while they are fractured, they are individually stronger on a comparable level, and their attacks reflect this. For example: a &quot;good guy&quot; werewolf pack will face vampires, crazed mages, Wyrm spirits, fomori, myriad others, and take them all down, usually with some violence. But playing a &quot;bad guy&quot; Pentex-executive game, one has werewolves attacking warehouses, vampires attempting hostile corporate takeovers, mages stealing or destroying technology, wraiths haunting the actors of the dietary supplement commercials that led to their death, weird fairy-tale people who seem to have some undefined grudge, dudes with flaming baseball bats attacking your soldiers... All while still having to pay off government officials, balance the quarterly budget, and attend the ribbon-cutting ceremony for some low-income housing.<br /> <br /> Basically, the bad guys work together because they have no morals or ethics.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:49:56-07:00","id":712401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=709847#post709847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More so why do people feel the need to play Y when the rest of the group is playing X in X setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because your group refuses to play Y even though you bought all the Y books and are super excited about Y? I played a Fae in a vampire game, he was eventually embraced and became a Kiasyd, but since my group would never play Fae in a hundred years (forget run Fae so I could actually PC), it was a blast for me to finally get to play one. I of course designed a fae who would fit in with the characters and setting (Winter court, sunlight as an echo).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:46:27-07:00","id":712608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=712401#post712401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe because your group refuses to play Y even though you bought all the Y books and are super excited about Y? I played a Fae in a vampire game, he was eventually embraced and became a Kiasyd, but since my group would never play Fae in a hundred years (forget run Fae so I could actually PC), it was a blast for me to finally get to play one. I of course designed a fae who would fit in with the characters and setting (Winter court, sunlight as an echo).</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point, I might consider finding another group. It may be an indicator that your tastes are so strongly at odds with everyone else's that the game you'd be comfortable having won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:42:00-07:00","id":712678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=710905#post710905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Liam mentioned Pentex twice when he posed the initial question. Thats why I mentioned it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> LIan. WIth an N. I am not an oathbreaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously I bring this up because I watch stuff like Being Human, which while not 1 for 1 WOD did play up the issues of various monster socieities interacting. So If I said I wanted to run a game about outcast supernaturals who band together on the edges or a family that has to deal with being torn apart by mixed ties and the drives of each(Kinfolk gets embraced/awakens and then what happens). But no one finds the very idea that everyone can set asside their insane evil for a basic paycheck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:45:12-07:00","id":712699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=712401#post712401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe because your group refuses to play Y even though you bought all the Y books and are super excited about Y? I played a Fae in a vampire game, he was eventually embraced and became a Kiasyd, but since my group would never play Fae in a hundred years (forget run Fae so I could actually PC), it was a blast for me to finally get to play one. I of course designed a fae who would fit in with the characters and setting (Winter court, sunlight as an echo).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the situation in which everyone in your group really likes playing X, but for whatever reason, one player isn't comfortable with the idea. For example, I love Demon, but I have a few players who really are not comfortable with the idea of playing one for various reasons. I know of other people who have issues with the pseudo-sexual violation aspects in Vampire. Sometimes those issues are insurmountable, but other times, you have players who might not mind playing a game themed around that particular group so long as they didn't have to play one. (Ghouls and thralls are options, but that often leaves them at the mercy of the other players, which isn't necessarily going to help them feel more comfortable with the game.)<br /> <br /> It's generally worth the extra effort to ensure that your players actually get to have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":"makes my statement make a little more sense. 10-21-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:19:58-07:00","id":712850,"title":"","content":"Well there's the thing that there are no &quot;good guy&quot; splats. You're not playing a street side vigilante, you're playing a monster who's trying to blend in with humanity while satisfying your urge to feed and personal agendas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:40:51-07:00","id":712873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=712608#post712608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At that point, I might consider finding another group. It may be an indicator that your tastes are so strongly at odds with everyone else's that the game you'd be comfortable having won't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For one thing, finding a new group isn't exactly easy. For another, my group is my friends who I have been friends with for 10-30 years and grew up with, not gonna just leave em. We've played several Vamp chronicles though and while none of them have any interest in Fae there was no reason for one chronicle not to allow me to play a Fae character. Also, finding a group that plays Dark Ages Fae (even a skype group or something) is pretty much impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:22:03-07:00","id":745944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable#post709808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kin mage, the &quot;good&quot; vampire, etc various explanations given for crossover is often mocked as &quot;Super friends' yet the Sabbat hanging out with Pentex, Nephandi just working for Pentex? these are just treated as &quot;reasonable&quot; forms of crossover? Why shouldn't the &quot;bad guys&quot; be just as prone to fracturing? Why aren't they as petty and short sighted in their attempts at destruction as anyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I find the Sabbat/Pentex alliance pretty silly. It's a relic of an earlier characterization of the Sabbat, where they were generic Evil(tm). I really think given the &quot;purge&quot; of infernalists from the Sabbat (the in-setting justification for the characterization change), Zettler should be portrayed as having lost his Sabbat connections and being harbored by his Pentex resources. The Sabbat/BSD joint-packs should go away completely as a setting &quot;thing&quot;. <br /> <br /> All that said, the reason Pentex, <i><b>Malfean</b></i> Nephandi, and various cultists of other supernatural types can believably work together is because they share common masters who may command it. That said sectarian holy war between Wyrm-worshipers is also rich narrative ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:59:19-07:00","id":745992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=745944#post745944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I find the Sabbat/Pentex alliance pretty silly. It's a relic of an earlier characterization of the Sabbat, where they were generic Evil(tm)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Sabbat in general would never work with a bunch of demon-worshipers. Individual vampires of both sects certainly would, but there wouldn't be any sect-specific tendencies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:04:44-08:00","id":746137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why shouldn't the &quot;bad guys&quot; be just as prone to fracturing? Why aren't they as petty and short sighted in their attempts at destruction as anyone else? </div> </div> </div>I think part of this has to do with these bad guys being controlled by powerful evil entities (the Wyrm, Oblivion, etc.) which are all more or less reflections of the same thing. *Humans* are a fractious lot. But when we talk about the *forces* that are at the core of these groups, we generally aren't talking about people anymore, so we can't ascribe human foibles to them. While it is hard to imagine a group such as the Nephandi being real (Let's destroy everything! Because... reasons!), the existence of the Caul and the dark forces of destruction that guide them not only make such a group possible, but also makes any alliance with similar groups believable as well. Their existence itself is already a 'gimme' as it is.<br /> <br /> As for the protagonists, they are supposed to be human. And they are also supposed to be largely ignorant of one another, being at the bottom of the conspiracy ladder, whereas the baddies tend more toward the top of the pyramid. They don't have benefit of our knowledge either... &quot;Did you see that? That looked like a changeling power! She must be a Sidhe or something!&quot; Um, no. It's not like you went to &quot;supernatural people night school&quot; or something. It sort of makes the &quot;super friends&quot; scenario a little bit improbable, at least at first. But then again, we are playing a game about vampires and werewolves, and the whole point is to have fun, so whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:48:05-08:00","id":754622,"title":"","content":"Yes this is why my thing about Salubri warring with some shadow lords for using disease as a weapon... to show that just because your both good guys, in your own way, doesnt mean you see eye to eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:51:44-08:00","id":754627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=754622#post754622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes this is why my thing about Salubri warring with some shadow lords for using disease as a weapon... to show that just because your both good guys, in your own way, doesnt mean you see eye to eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using biological warfare doesn't tend to be the bag of most Garou. Now, Ratkin, on the other hand, that's a big part of their reason for being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:35:11-08:00","id":754776,"title":"","content":"I'd agree... but , in roman times when a shadowlord sept is in danger of being over ran be human expansion.... I think they may see biological warfare as a valid solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:57:30-08:00","id":755409,"title":"","content":"Tossing dead bodies into another guys city was a valid and recognized siege tactic back then.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T20:48:17-08:00","id":755792,"title":"","content":"There was a bit I was reading in the Revised Book of Madness about how, from the Werewolves' perspective, all the forces of corruption come from the Wyrm - not just figuratively, but literally. it also laid out a canonical metaplot explanation for the forces behind the Nephandi, no matter their breed, and how those forces were the dreams and emanations of the Neverborn, which meant that, if you used that explanation in your Mage game, the so-called Wyrm and Maeljin were incarnations of the Neverborn's dreams (since the Malfean Nephandi worshipped the Maeljin Incarnae, and all Nephandi's objects of worship were placed under that clause). I 'm hoping (and think this is the case) that this is no longer canon, but both of those interpretations allow for the forces of evil to all be working together because they all have the same bosses with different email addresses.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a useful storytelling device, especially for storytellers who have players that want a bit of everything. Rather than have to come up with individual plots for each villain, they can work together to achieve the same aim, cutting down on potentially overwhelming amounts of plot for the players to deal with/chase. If the outcome is reasonable to all involved parties, even if the reasons come from different places for each, it makes sense that they would agree to work together, at least for a little while, to achieve their mutual interest. It just so happens that the interests of the bad guys line up more often than those of the good guys (especially when the good guys have a reason to hate all the bad guys, like the Garou do with vampires, mages, hunters... pretty much everyone actually).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:53:50-08:00","id":757496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=755409#post755409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tossing dead bodies into another guys city was a valid and recognized siege tactic back then.....</div> </div> </div> </div>For humans, yes. Garou have more concerns than just &quot;break the siege&quot;, and tend to be incredibly stuck up about using disease and/or poison instead of waging war. The fact that it might actually result in an Honor hit is one of those reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:32:37-08:00","id":757624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=757496#post757496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For humans, yes. Garou have more concerns than just &amp;quot;break the siege&amp;quot;, and tend to be incredibly stuck up about using disease and/or poison instead of waging war. The fact that it might actually result in an Honor hit is one of those reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing how as the tribe in question is the shadow lords.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:08:11-08:00","id":758177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=757624#post757624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeing how as the tribe in question is the shadow lords.....</div> </div> </div> </div>lt's still not something most Shadow Lords would do. That's why I can see a desperate Shadow Lord who is on his way to corruption doing it as a warning tale, but I'd still say that he's an exception rather then the rule among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T03:54:52-08:00","id":758381,"title":"","content":"Shadow Lords always get a bad rep just because they're sinister and a bit creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T04:29:36-08:00","id":758426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=758381#post758381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Lords always get a bad rep just because they're sinister and a bit creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not sinister and creepy. That's the Uktena and Wendigo hat. Shadow Lords just get the bad rep for being sneaky backstabbers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T04:56:24-08:00","id":758443,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, although I did say a <i>bit</i> creepy. Uktena get the full-on creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:26:46-08:00","id":758628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/709808-why-are-super-friends-mocked-but-the-legion-of-doom-considered-reasonable?p=757624#post757624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeing how as the tribe in question is the shadow lords.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the &quot;stuck up&quot; part still applies. They may not have the breeding restrictions of the Silver Fangs, but they do adhere to decorum and protocol codes that are restrictive in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}